   - **Note on prior ruling:** The writer implemented the literal `C1` ruling as written (gating [`legacy_run_id_proven`](file:///Users/0x/Projects/hornhoof-edge/relay/relay.py#L335-L346) on `online == True`, which closes all live-session takeovers). However, testing the absent/offline path against real `frps` 0.71.1 exposes a cross-binding `clientID`-squatting bypass.
   - **What is wrong:** [`CLIENT.fullmatch(run_id)`](file:///Users/0x/Projects/hornhoof-edge/relay/relay.py#L342) is checked only inside [`legacy_run_id_proven`](file:///Users/0x/Projects/hornhoof-edge/relay/relay.py#L335-L346) when `/api/clients?runId=` already reports an `online` session ([`relay/relay.py:330`](file:///Users/0x/Projects/hornhoof-edge/relay/relay.py#L330)). When `globex-<m8>-link` (or `-peer` / `-visit`) is not yet online, a legacy `Login` (`client_id == ""`) authenticated with `acme`'s key and `run_id = "globex-3f2a9c1b-link"` passes [`client_id_reason`](file:///Users/0x/Projects/hornhoof-edge/relay/relay.py#L635-L648), [`run_id_recorded_elsewhere`](file:///Users/0x/Projects/hornhoof-edge/relay/relay.py#L349-L358), and [`run_id_conflict`](file:///Users/0x/Projects/hornhoof-edge/relay/relay.py#L307-L332). Because `frps` 0.71.1 sets `clientID = client_id or run_id`, `frps` registers `acme`'s session online under `clientID = "globex-3f2a9c1b-link"`, bypassing cross-binding client-ID isolation (`this client id is not for acme`) and locking out `globex` on a shared-`m8` machine (R1.4). Live sessions cannot be displaced and `globex` routes/services cannot be offered by `acme`.
   - **Reproduction:** Bind `acme` and `globex` on a local `Stack`; open [`FrpsWireSession`](file:///Users/0x/Projects/hornhoof-edge/relay/test/test_peers.py#L708-L796) with `metas={'name': 'acme', 'key': acme_key}`, `client_id=''`, `run_id='globex-3f2a9c1b-link'`. `Login` is accepted (`accepted == True`), `/api/clients` shows `clientID == 'globex-3f2a9c1b-link'` online, and starting legitimate `globex` `frpc` (`client='globex-3f2a9c1b-link'`) fails with `client [globex-3f2a9c1b-link] is already online`.
   - **What would make it right:** Reject `not client_id and CLIENT.fullmatch(run_id)` unconditionally in [`login_reason`](file:///Users/0x/Projects/hornhoof-edge/relay/relay.py#L676-L681) (before [`run_id_conflict`](file:///Users/0x/Projects/hornhoof-edge/relay/relay.py#L307-L332), regardless of `online`) with `'this run id belongs to another client'` (or `f'this client id is not for {name}'`), and add a native wire test proving `acme` cannot squat `globex-3f2a9c1b-link` while `globex` is offline. Genuine `frps`-assigned legacy `run_id`s are `[0-9a-f]{16}` and never match `CLIENT`, so offline legacy reconnects stay unchanged with no session registry or wire-format change.

